      "content": "<!-- docspress:{\"version\":1,\"key\":\"docs\",\"source\":\"examples/contextual-sidebars/docs/index.md\",\"hash\":\"5d32dc2acb58db7b6c2df79f01ae282df3c012a917b835b2dfa89f111e29bd2c\",\"sourceContentBase64\":\"\",\"sidebarPosition\":0,\"sidebarCollapsed\":false,\"sidebarId\":\"docs\",\"sidebarRoot\":true} -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This example keeps general guides in the default documentation sidebar while API and extension Pages receive focused navigation trees.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Read the <a href=\"/docs/guides/quickstart/\">quickstart</a>, browse the <a href=\"/docs/apis/rest-api/\">REST API</a>, or <a href=\"/docs/extensions/build-an-extension/\">build an extension</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
